  "scientific_limits": [
    "Cuenca Omas code 1375512 is an official hydrologic unit, but the current IRFEN compound candidate also references local Asia ravines and coastal fans that are not yet individually normalized.",
    "RD 0312-2022 is a regulatory faja-marginal source for a bounded Omas-Río Chico de Asia reach and branch; it is not a flood footprint, full-basin polygon or observed hydraulic capacity.",
    "The 2016 vulnerable-population map identifies exposure around Quebrada Río Chico but does not supply a normalized exposure layer in this package.",
    "INGEMMET 2017 documents hazard/impact sites in the Asia-Omas corridor but does not establish a complete dated event ledger with primary hydrometeorological observations.",
    "COEN-INDECI record 190014 confirms a huaico in Asia district on 2024-02-06, but the source excerpt does not assign that event to Río Omas, Río Chico or a specific local ravine.",
    "No verified hydrologic negative control is created.",
    "No faja-marginal width, critical-point rating, impact description or event registration is promoted into an IRFEN threshold."
  ],
  "accepted_research_uses": [
    "official Cuenca Omas identity and named-watercourse discovery",
    "partial regulatory geometry discovery",
    "Río Chico exposure discovery",
    "district-level and corridor-level positive hazard context",
    "prioritization of named-ravine, outlet-fan and observation acquisition"
  ],
  "forbidden_uses": [
    "operational threshold derivation",
    "automatic alerting",
    "treating regulatory faja marginal as event footprint",
    "assigning the 2024 Asia huaico to Río Omas or Río Chico without source evidence",
    "merging all Asia ravines into Cuenca Omas without hydrologic validation",
    "negative-control inference from missing reports",
    "approving or activating the Asia-Omas Phase-2 contract"
  ]
